DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/<database>?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require
# Connection string for a SEPARATE, isolated Neon branch used only by
# postgres-store.test.ts, which truncates every table before each test case.
# Must never be the same database as DATABASE_URL. Create an isolated branch
# with Neon's branching feature (free, instant, copy-on-write) — see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-persistent-storage-design.md — and paste
# that branch's connection string here. The test suite refuses to run (and
# does not connect to any database) if this is unset or identical to
# DATABASE_URL.
COMPANION_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/<database>?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# Number of reverse proxies/load balancers in front of this relay. Required everywhere except
# local development/test (NODE_ENV=development or NODE_ENV=test) — the relay refuses to start
# without it, because there is no safe default: 0 behind a real proxy and non-zero with no proxy
# are each silently wrong in the other's environment, and either one breaks per-IP rate limiting
# for pairing/registration. An unset NODE_ENV counts as "not local dev/test", so this is also
# required if your deployment doesn't explicitly set NODE_ENV=production. Left commented out
# here deliberately — do NOT uncomment this with a guessed value; set it to the real hop count
# for your deployment (0 only if you are certain there is no proxy in front).
# COMPANION_RELAY_TRUST_PROXY=
# Comma-separated list of origins allowed to call this relay from a browser (the web app's own
# origin(s)). Unset defaults to http://localhost:5173 (Vite's default dev port) only.
COMPANION_RELAY_CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# Optional, comma-separated list of extra bare hostnames (no scheme/path/port/IP literals)
# allowed as Web Push subscription endpoints, on top of the built-in browser vendor hosts. Only
# needed if a push provider isn't already recognized by packages/protocol/src/push.ts. Fails
# fast at startup (when the allowlist is first validated) if set but malformed. Unset is fine.
# COMPANION_RELAY_PUSH_ENDPOINT_ALLOWLIST=
